    "SIGNIFICANT (NEW) — RGFL (arXiv 2601.18044, Jan 2026) is absent from the landscape and directly competes: 'Reasoning Guided Fault Localization for Automated Program Repair Using LLMs' integrates a hierarchical reasoning module with Agentless to generate structured, bug-specific explanations for candidate files, achieving Hit@1 improvement from 71.4%→85% and 12.8% end-to-end repair success improvement on Agentless. This is a direct competitor on the core localization improvement claim and was available since January 2026 — EMNLP reviewers will flag its absence. SpecExtract must differentiate from RGFL: (1) RGFL uses per-instance LLM reasoning at localization time (high inference cost), while SpecExtract's spec extraction is a single forward pass of a fine-tuned model; (2) RGFL generates file-level explanations, not typed behavioral specs (affected interface, expected behavior, delta) that constrain patch generation; (3) RGFL does not address the 'ambiguous issue description' structural limitation that motivates issue-space extraction. These differentiations exist but must be stated explicitly.",
